  "gesture": "You reach past the windowsill and pull your coat off the hook by the door, shaking it once so the fabric settles, then drape it over your forearm while you lean against the payphone.",
  "words": "Rita, I'm not arguing the clock again. I need the weather copy done, Larry to cut the lights, and me at that depot before one. You tell me when we roll and I'll be there. That's the whole deal.",
  "intention": "Lock down the shoot time with Rita now so I walk out of here with a clear deadline and a ticket in my pocket, and I'm on that coach by twelve-fifteen."
